  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.2.1
The National Workers&apos; Committee (NWC) developed a national strategy to expand its membership through organizing workers&apos; committees at enterprise level. In addition, a communication strategy was held in an effort to protect workers against the COVID-19 pandemic, also a strategy to organize workers.

1.2.2
The Kingdom of Saudi Arabia (KSA) National Workers&apos; Committee (NWC), actively engaged in the effort to establish social dialogue in KSA on the basis of international labour standards. 1.2.1
ILO provided technical support to develop a new staretgy to expand its membership through targeting selected economic sectors and regions of the country, including enhanced cooperation with employers.
ILO provided technical support to NWC to conduct awareness-raising campaigns through social media, including posters and meetings on COVID-19, and protection measures in workplaces. The campaign aimed at mobilizing and organize new groups of workers, including migrant workers.

1.2.2
ILO provided training: 
- for NWC leaders through a workshop in March 2020 on basic social dialogue concepts, key preconditions, including freedom of association and the right to collective bargaining, as well as variety of practices of social dialogue at the national level, and social dialogue in the ILO.
- for NCW leaders (online by ITCILO) on enhancing social dialogue mechanisms for better policy formulation in KSA. 

ILO also supported workers&apos; organizations to build the capacity of its leaders, through regional webinars/trainings implemented for the Arab Trade Union Organization in May, June, July and December 2020, and in February, June, and July 2021. The activities focused on the impact of COVID-19 on workers and the role of trade unions during the crisis.

ILO provided technical support to lead the W20 Group meetings during the KSA presidency of G20 as well as to participate in the preparatory meetings held by the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Development (MHRSD) prior to the 11th National Dialogue Forum on Social Dialogue in October 2021.</narrative>
   </description>
